{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1230171-razor-wire-gloves-artifact-or-martial-art","id":1230171,"title":"Razor Wire Gloves - artifact or martial art?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-06-25T20:36:32-07:00","id":1230171,"title":"Razor Wire Gloves - artifact or martial art?","content":"Anyone ever watched <i>Hellsing's </i>Walter Dorneaz, or any other anime character fight with gloves trailing unbreakable, razor-sharp mono-filament wires that cut through anything they can loop around, and loop around anything without regard for physics?<br /> <br /> Some character like him was surely the inspiration for Charcoal March of Spider Style's Rain of Unseen Threads and Nest of Living Strands Charms.<br /> <br /> I propose that these could be starmetal artifact gloves which, as an attunement bonus, can be used as a razor-wire garrote. Its Evocations would basically be Rain of Unseen Threads and Nest of Living Strands, only cut apart into multiple, not-overpowered Charms. Including one for feats of destruction against the environment (cutting apart rafters, pillars, and trees).<br /> <br /> If Charcoal March of Spiders still keeps those Charms, then the gloves' master would find them easier to use with the gloves.<br /> <br /> Other Evocations might let the master use clinched or incapacitated enemies into human puppets to turn against their allies. Which Walter also did, but which Charcoal March of Spiders never quite allowed. Maybe using the gloves with Throne Shadow Style would help you direct the actions of your shadow-fingers similar to how that one old Sand Kunoichi helped Sakura fight Sasori?<br /> <br /> Using the wires for practical telekinesis might let you make Melee at a range... and at a <i>greater</i> range, for Thrown weapons. <i>Touhou Project's</i> Alice Margatroid loves fighting people with dolls armed with live blades.<br /> <br /> <br /> Unless you think that turning a garrote into magically improbable witch-floss is better for a whole Martial Arts Style than a specific pair of gloves?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-26T00:39:54-07:00","id":1230209,"title":"","content":"I think that Walter's gloves and wires would be best done as an artefact, as you said. I've been mulling over a 'Spider Style' for a while, basically being a 'spy style' that uses essence-imbued threads, but it's much more centred around A) binding opponents, B) setting traps with thread C) using threads for mobility (e.g. grapples, running along threads far above the ground etc) and D) using threads as spying tools (e.g. running a thread near someone you want to eavesdrop on and listening to the vibrations).<br /> <br /> Another possible source for inspiration for wire-fighting styles or charms could be Yura of the Demon Hair, from one of the early episodes (I think it's about the 5th?) if the anime <i>Inuyasha.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-26T06:40:06-07:00","id":1230262,"title":"","content":"* Garrote on demand<br /> * Grapple at a distance<br /> * Restrain and cause damage with distant grapple<br /> * Pull self to enemy or self to enemy<br /> * Snare rafters and stuff to climb or swing around<br /> * Disarm at a distance, potentially destroying a mundane weapon<br /> * Clash attack against projectiles<br /> * Pick stuff up and move it around<br /> * Attack with stuff you\u2019ve picked up<br /> * Manipulate a corpse to use your Abilities, including any Martial Arts you know<br /> * Manipulate a cooperating minion<br /> * Manipulate a restrained grappling victim<br /> <br /> That sounds like a lot for an Artifact, but plenty for a Spider Style Martial Art Style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-26T07:08:37-07:00","id":1230272,"title":"","content":"Our White Veil Style Night Caste has a Statmetal &amp; Moonsilver Artifact partially based on Walters Razor Wire Gloves; though we took it off in another direction to allow for the control and puppeteering of targets.<br /> <br /> If I get the chance I'll pull it up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-26T08:36:55-07:00","id":1230293,"title":"","content":"First Pre-Form: When stunting the use of magically extended wires for the purpose of climbing or swinging from things, convert stunt dice to successes on movement actions or attacks made while swinging<br /> <br /> Second Pre-Form: Perform gambits against targets at short range<br /> <br /> Form: Use wires to manipulate objects at short range for actions and attacks, including clashes with manipulated objects<br /> <br /> Post Form a1: Clash projectiles better<br /> <br /> Post Form a2: Feats of Destruction<br /> <br /> Post Form b3: extend range<br /> <br /> Post Form b4: grasp multiple objects with wires<br /> <br /> Post Form c5: act through ally<br /> <br /> Post Form c6: puppet corpse (like the effects of the Form Charm, but enemies have to disengage from the corpse like they don\u2019t have to against a wire-controlled sword)<br /> <br /> Pinnacle: Control restrained enemy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-26T10:07:14-07:00","id":1230314,"title":"","content":"Damn. I forgot Nest of Living Strands. That\u2019s at least another Charm or two for the Style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-26T10:13:50-07:00","id":1230315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1230171-razor-wire-gloves-artifact-or-martial-art?p=1230293#post1230293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First Pre-Form: When stunting the use of magically extended wires for the purpose of climbing or swinging from things, convert stunt dice to successes on movement actions or attacks made while swinging<br /> <br /> Second Pre-Form: Perform gambits against targets at short range<br /> <br /> Form: Use wires to manipulate objects at short range for actions and attacks, including clashes with manipulated objects<br /> <br /> Post Form a1: Clash projectiles better<br /> <br /> Post Form a2: Feats of Destruction<br /> <br /> Post Form b3: extend range<br /> <br /> Post Form b4: grasp multiple objects with wires<br /> <br /> Post Form c5: act through ally<br /> <br /> Post Form c6: puppet corpse (like the effects of the Form Charm, but enemies have to disengage from the corpse like they don\u2019t have to against a wire-controlled sword)<br /> <br /> Pinnacle: Control restrained enemy</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Reminds me of my Emerald Wasp style with those Pinnacles. Let me know how it goes! I think it could be terrifying and cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-26T10:19:48-07:00","id":1230319,"title":"","content":"If it were an Exigent you could keep iterating new stuff indefinitely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-26T11:20:23-07:00","id":1230330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1230171-razor-wire-gloves-artifact-or-martial-art?p=1230319#post1230319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it were an Exigent you could keep iterating new stuff indefinitely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Chosen of Strings, Exigent of Stone Free, the god of threads: Jolyne Cujoh.<br /> <br /> JoJo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-26T12:11:02-07:00","id":1230341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Janissary87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1230171-razor-wire-gloves-artifact-or-martial-art?p=1230272#post1230272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Our White Veil Style Night Caste has a Statmetal &amp; Moonsilver Artifact partially based on Walters Razor Wire Gloves; though we took it off in another direction to allow for the control and puppeteering of targets.<br /> <br /> If I get the chance I'll pull it up.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I really would like to read about it, as though I would like to see the mechanics of the gloves of <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar636_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"636\" data-vbnamecard=\"636\">Sunder the Gold</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12575-gaara","name":"Gaara","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-26T21:41:20-07:00","id":1230462,"title":"","content":"Long ago I made an artifact called Web of Silent Release based on the same inspiration. Back then, it was pretty much long ranged Razor Claws with Artful Maiming Onslaught built in. It would be fun to revisit with Evocations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T05:49:22-07:00","id":1230513,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m thinking Nest of Living Strands could actually be a pre-form Charm if you reduce its power enough.<br /> <br /> At first, the Charm requires the user to prepare the trap before combat begins, and its primary effect is to wither an opponent\u2019s Initiative to build the martial artist up for those ranged gambits. <br /> <br /> The movement enhancing Charm could be post-form, considering how it might build upon ranges grapples to pull victims closer, or into the air (with leverage), or pull you closer to them. <br /> <br /> Other Charms in the Style, auto-upgrades, and Mastery effects can make Nest of Living Strands something quicker and more impressive to use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T10:00:00-07:00","id":1230573,"title":"","content":"The puppeteering Charm offers a lot of fun potential.<br /> <br /> You could just use any corpse you find (or produce), or you could use a literal manikin that you keep around for just such a purpose.<br /> <br /> You could make artifact manikins loaded with hidden weapons, like Gaara\u2019s brother and Sasori. Each one represented by an Evocation.<br /> <br /> You could have a replacement Evocation to trade places with your puppet. <br /> <br /> These puppets could have Evocations that assist your efforts to disguise them to look like you, or other people. Use the Solar ventriloquism Charm to make it seem like you\u2019re speaking through it.<br /> <br /> Another Evocation would work like a less \u201cbullshit\u201d form of Dual Magnus Prana. If one has used sufficient Awareness magic previously in the scene, then you can reveal \u201cyou\u201d were your puppet the entire time, while the real you was hidden safely around the corner. (This also requires that you had a sufficient hiding place that no one checked previously in the scene.)<br /> <br /> You could also say \u201cfuck subtlety\u201d and build an artifact puppet as big as a warstrider, and control it like Giant Robo, only with puppet strings instead of a radio watch. Alice Margatroid\u2019s \u201cGoliath Doll\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T10:09:53-07:00","id":1230578,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t think Puppeteer Spider Style would need a venom Charm to complete its concept or strategy, but it would definitely be a tool used more often than puppets.<br /> <br /> The more penalties a target suffers, the easier they are to surprise, ensnare, and control.<br /> <br /> Of course, those Sand Ninja puppeteers loved their poisons, and their puppets had Evocations for poison gas, poison needles, poison blades...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T10:12:15-07:00","id":1230579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1230171-razor-wire-gloves-artifact-or-martial-art?p=1230319#post1230319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it were an Exigent you could keep iterating new stuff indefinitely.</div> </div> </div> </div>The point at which this exigent starts snaring the threads of the loom of fate with their fingers is the moment the Sidereals come to put them to rest.<br /> <br /> ...Side note: Pattern Spider exigent","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/357-plotvitalnpc","name":"PlotVitalNPC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar357_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T10:15:27-07:00","id":1230580,"title":"","content":"I figure such an Exigent (either one) would learn this martial art style as a bunch of native Charms, and the form would be more of a permanent Charm without the form tag.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T15:49:43-07:00","id":1230663,"title":"","content":"Other wire stylists for inspiration include: Jenos Hazard from Black Cat (His glove is actually made from Orichalcum in world)<br /> <a href=\"http://blackcat.wikia.com/wiki/Jenos_Hazard\" target=\"_blank\">http://blackcat.wikia.com/wiki/Jenos_Hazard</a><br /> And Kasuki of the Strings from GetBackers (He(?) uses a combination of this style and Nightingale style)<br /> <a href=\"http://getbackers.wikia.com/wiki/Kazuki_Fuuchouin\" target=\"_blank\">http://getbackers.wikia.com/wiki/Kazuki_Fuuchouin</a><br /> <br /> Honestly, I think this concept could easily form the basis of one or more Artifacts, a Martial Arts style, and an Exigent or two, depending on where you take it. It should probably be more focused in an Artifact, but any at rank 4 or above can have theoretically any number of Evocations, so really, worry less about which one is the \u201ccorrect\u201d way to translate this effect over and focus on creating the thing you WANT to make.<br /> <br /> Regardless, I look forward to seeing what you come up with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T16:11:25-07:00","id":1230675,"title":"","content":"Only one person can use an artifact, but with a martial art you can at least have a duel.<br /> <br /> If you nail down the martial art first, you can then go on to make as many artifacts as you want to embellish and twist the common body of techniques.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T17:20:12-07:00","id":1230689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1230171-razor-wire-gloves-artifact-or-martial-art?p=1230675#post1230675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only one person can use an artifact, but with a martial art you can at least have a duel.<br /> <br /> If you nail down the martial art first, you can then go on to make as many artifacts as you want to embellish and twist the common body of techniques.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, puppeteering people always felt like sidereal throne extension charms. Which in 3e would be brawl over ma. If they still keep the singular ability to create extension charms for that style.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T18:07:29-07:00","id":1230700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1230171-razor-wire-gloves-artifact-or-martial-art?p=1230689#post1230689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, puppeteering people always felt like sidereal throne extension charms. Which in 3e would be brawl over ma. If they still keep the singular ability to create extension charms for that style.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereal Brawl doesn't include manipulation or threads as a theme, and Throne Shadow Style is about guiding the willing rather than controlling one's enemies.<br /> <br /> But Throne Shadow doesn't use strings, and it has a much stronger focus on guidance and assistance than Puppeteer Spider, which only diverges into that with a single Charm that only serves as a logical stepping stone between &quot;control a lifeless corpse&quot; and &quot;control a resisting enemy&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T18:14:50-07:00","id":1230705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1230171-razor-wire-gloves-artifact-or-martial-art?p=1230700#post1230700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sidereal Brawl doesn't include manipulation or threads as a theme, and Throne Shadow Style is about guiding the willing rather than controlling one's enemies.<br /> <br /> But Throne Shadow doesn't use strings, and it has a much stronger focus on guidance and assistance than Puppeteer Spider, which only diverges into that with a single Charm that only serves as a logical stepping stone between &amp;quot;control a lifeless corpse&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;control a resisting enemy&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Looking at the way hero styles branched off in previous editions. It wouldn't be a big leap to create charms that control willing or unwilling fingers. They wouldn't directly show puppet strings but it would still be direct control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T18:20:46-07:00","id":1230707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1230171-razor-wire-gloves-artifact-or-martial-art?p=1230705#post1230705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking at the way hero styles branched off in previous editions. It wouldn't be a big leap to create charms that control willing or unwilling fingers. They wouldn't directly show puppet strings but it would still be direct control.</div> </div> </div> </div>By that same logic, we could expect a Solar Brawl version of Fivefold Bulwark Stance. Which we didn't and won't get, because such comprehensive defense runs against the themes of Solar Brawl.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T18:29:43-07:00","id":1230710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1230171-razor-wire-gloves-artifact-or-martial-art?p=1230707#post1230707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By that same logic, we could expect a Solar Brawl version of Fivefold Bulwark Stance. Which we didn't and won't get, because such comprehensive defense runs against the themes of Solar Brawl.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really the same thing. The themes of control and manipulation are intrisic to sidereal throne style.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T19:02:12-07:00","id":1230714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1230171-razor-wire-gloves-artifact-or-martial-art?p=1230710#post1230710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The themes of control and manipulation are intrisic to sidereal throne style.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't say this often, but I'm with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar636_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"636\" data-vbnamecard=\"636\">Sunder the Gold</a> on this one. While Bulwark Stance might not be the best analogy, he's still right in that there's only so far a theme should really be allowed to stretch, and &quot;manipulate others through the trappings of the wise instructor&quot; mutating into &quot;directly control people's bodies with strings&quot; is about nine leagues past the acceptable point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T19:05:17-07:00","id":1230715,"title":"","content":"Donquixote Doflamingo from One Piece at the ito-ito no mi, the thread-thread fruit. He is basically tvtropes' Razor Floss: the man. That page is a good idea for inspiration. <br /> <br /> I like the idea of a pattern spider exigent- someone like a &quot;sidereal lite&quot; who deals with snags in the loom and tries to ease the workload of the spiders. <br /> <br /> People puppets fits the theme, since you are a thread master. Id venture there should be a bonus on disarming and a bonus on dis-arming people. <br /> <br /> Sorta related but i'm working on a razor-whip for an npc. It can attack out to Short and is flexible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T19:05:44-07:00","id":1230717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1230171-razor-wire-gloves-artifact-or-martial-art?p=1230714#post1230714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't say this often, but I'm with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar636_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"636\" data-vbnamecard=\"636\">Sunder the Gold</a> on this one. While Bulwark Stance might not be the best analogy, he's still right in that there's only so far a theme should really be allowed to stretch, and &quot;manipulate others through the trappings of the wise instructor&quot; mutating into &quot;directly control people's bodies with strings&quot; is about nine leagues past the acceptable point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Controlling people with the invisible strings of fate is entirely within their theme though. This would just be a natural extension of using charms through fingers as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T19:09:37-07:00","id":1230718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1230171-razor-wire-gloves-artifact-or-martial-art?p=1230714#post1230714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't say this often, but I'm with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar636_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"636\" data-vbnamecard=\"636\">Sunder the Gold</a> on this one.</div> </div> </div> </div>One can find a bar of gold in any trash can.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1230171-razor-wire-gloves-artifact-or-martial-art?p=1230717#post1230717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Controlling people with the invisible strings of fate is entirely within their theme though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, and that's why they have Sidereal Astrology.<br /> <br /> But the Gauntlet's message is &quot;Survival is Fury&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 06-27-2018, 10:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T19:16:12-07:00","id":1230723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1230171-razor-wire-gloves-artifact-or-martial-art?p=1230718#post1230718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Yeah, and that's why they have Sidereal Astrology.<br /> <br /> But the Gauntlet's message is &quot;Survival is Fury&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>The guantlet isn't the constellation used for this style. Have you seen the style recently? Moving to more direct control is easily within the themes of the style.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T19:23:22-07:00","id":1230724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1230171-razor-wire-gloves-artifact-or-martial-art?p=1230723#post1230723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The guantlet isn't the constellation used for this style. Have you seen the style recently? Moving to more direct control is easily within the themes of the style.</div> </div> </div> </div>Throne Shadow Style will be a closed Style incapable of expansion. Which is good, since the First Edition Brawl Charms still made a poor fit for it.<br /> <br /> Throne Shadow has quite enough going on already that it doesn't need string-fu tricks, and there are so many string-fu tricks to use that they can be their own style.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, I want to talk about what sort of effects are appropriately tame for Puppeteer Spider's pre-Form Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T19:25:09-07:00","id":1230725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1230171-razor-wire-gloves-artifact-or-martial-art?p=1230724#post1230724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Throne Shadow Style will be a closed Style incapable of expansion. Which is good, since the First Edition Brawl Charms still made a poor fit for it.<br /> <br /> Throne Shadow has quite enough going on already that it doesn't need string-fu tricks, and there are so many string-fu tricks to use that they can be their own style.</div> </div> </div> </div>How do you know that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T19:45:12-07:00","id":1230727,"title":"","content":"So, how about sources?<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Spider-Man's</i> Webshooters are an artifact with a lot of promise. Most if not all of the effects of the Distaff, plus plenty of its own! You could definitely use those to produce a garrote and strings for this Style, while at the same time this Style is completely separate from the Webshooter's natural Evocations, which normally produce more rope-like projectiles than string-like. More focused on mobility and capture than murder or manipulation.<br /> <br /> <i>Naruto's</i> Kankuro (finally remembered his name) and the other ninja generally used strings made of chakra/Essence; didn't use them for cutting or grappling anything, but for controlling their puppets.<br /> <br /> Sasuke used actual, physical wires. Threw a bunch of shuriken with wires attached to bind Orochimaru to a tree, and then shot flames down the wires to envelop and consume him. Maybe not quite this style so much as Solar Thrown's Whirlwind Hand of the Striker, though.<br /> <br /> It's been a long time since I read or watched <i>Black Cat</i>, so I'd need to brush up on Jenos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T19:51:07-07:00","id":1230728,"title":"","content":"So I've been playing with the idea of using some Exigents to express the puppet ninjas from the Naruto series into Exalted, expressed as Chosen of the God of Animated Figures. I never considered the razor wire concept for them as there is acton of cool stuff these powers do just in Naruto. And while the show lets true masters take control of live humans, i thought it a bit extreme for an Exalt type that players wpuld see the powers of. Instead i want to use them to make himan scale puppets, maybe golems come to life, mess with corpses to fake zombies, or at the clomax of fighting one, have to use a non-functional warstrider by sheer force of will.<br /> <br /> But this entire concept sits between the space of most razor wire powers/effects and the body possession idea that Throne Shadow Style considers within its purview.<br /> <br /> The most 'control' I would consider establishing would be the complete ambush rule where you have them in a social scene by having the wire wrapped around them, using those rounds of control as actions caused by a Threaten move (obvious bodily harm). Magic it up a bit to make it mechanically feasible and it sounds like a lot of fun","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24220-cryo-seraph","name":"Cryo-Seraph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T19:55:46-07:00","id":1230730,"title":"","content":"There is an adjoran demon that can control people using it's body i believe that charm is eclipse usable. Personally, i would keep it to an artifact 4-5 pair of gloves. I don't think it can fit an entire style. In addition to throne shadow style, I do think lunar charms would easily be able to replicate the fulope's control using manipulation charms and cordyceps. But I suppose the look of puppeteering someone is important.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 06-27-2018, 11:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T21:29:34-07:00","id":1230738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cryo-Seraph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1230171-razor-wire-gloves-artifact-or-martial-art?p=1230728#post1230728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And while the show lets true masters take control of live humans, i thought it a bit extreme for an Exalt type that players wpuld see the powers of.</div> </div> </div> </div>If those humans were mortals and &quot;insignificant/trivial opponents&quot;, it would be fine. The puppet-master ninja rarely (if ever) took direct control of their equal opponents.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the body possession idea that Throne Shadow Style considers within its purview. </div> </div> </div>Throne Shadow doesn't possess people. The most directly controlling thing it does is to pull the breath out of someone's lungs and use it as a chain or rope to clinch them.<br /> <br /> Most of Throne Shadow's tricks are to empower the martial artist's allies and minions, making them stronger and coordinating their efforts, but never actually dictating what they do.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1230171-razor-wire-gloves-artifact-or-martial-art?p=1230730#post1230730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, i would keep it to an artifact 4-5 pair of gloves. I don't think it can fit an entire style.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you not see the post where I laid out a full Martial Arts Charmset with the standard 10 Charms -- two pre-form, one Form, six post-form, and one pinnacle?<br /> <br /> And that's when I <i>forgot</i> some tricks I wanted to include.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 06-28-2018, 12:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-28T04:57:33-07:00","id":1230770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1230171-razor-wire-gloves-artifact-or-martial-art?p=1230738#post1230738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Throne Shadow doesn't possess people. The most directly controlling thing it does is to pull the breath out of someone's lungs and use it as a chain or rope to clinch them.<br /> <br /> Most of Throne Shadow's tricks are to empower the martial artist's allies and minions, making them stronger and coordinating their efforts, but never actually dictating what they do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except for the form charm which forces people to defend other for you or the second to last charm which forces enemy extras to be your shadow fingers. It also worked on automata at e4. There are a number of effects that were quite direct in that style. Leading to full possession would not be out theme for the style. A lot of hero charms branched out from what I remember.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Did you not see the post where I laid out a full Martial Arts Charmset with the standard 10 Charms -- two pre-form, one Form, six post-form, and one pinnacle?<br /> <br /> And that's when I <i>forgot</i> some tricks I wanted to include. </div> </div> </div>I did but i suppose it comes down to philosphy. Every time i remember the pinnacle of the puppeteering effects in anime. It always comes down to the sakura and chiyo fight. Where it feels like a sidereal controlling a solar to make her stronger than she could make herself. However, a lot of those effects are more powerful than a normal martial art. It also comes down to like 1-4 charms to put in every necessary effect. Charcoal march of spiders almost did everything in one charm as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-28T05:48:42-07:00","id":1230776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1230171-razor-wire-gloves-artifact-or-martial-art?p=1230770#post1230770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except for the form charm which forces people to defend other for you</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it ENABLES them to defend you. A player character can choose not to apply their Parry against any particular attack; NPCs are not generally afforded that choice because they're storyteller characters and their autonomy is less important.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the second to last charm which forces enemy extras to be your shadow fingers. </div> </div> </div>If by &quot;forces&quot; you mean &quot;persuades&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It also worked on automata at e4. </div> </div> </div>So the martial artist can convince robots just like Dawn Castes can intimidate robots. Magic!<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There are a number of effects that were quite direct in that style. </div> </div> </div>Now you're torturing my words.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Leading to full possession would not be out theme for the style. A lot of hero charms branched out from what I remember. </div> </div> </div>Completely irrelevant when there are no more &quot;hero styles&quot;!<br /> <br /> The base Style was complete already, and doesn't need a whole other Style tacked on.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I did but i suppose it comes down to philosphy. Every time i remember the pinnacle of the puppeteering effects in anime. It always comes down to the sakura and chiyo fight. Where it feels like a sidereal controlling a solar to make her stronger than she could make herself. </div> </div> </div>Chiyo wouldn't have been able to do that if Sakura had resisted.<br /> <br /> Therefore, the more powerful trick is using someone as a puppet when they don't want to be a puppet.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However, a lot of those effects are more powerful than a normal martial art. It also comes down to like 1-4 charms to put in every necessary effect. </div> </div> </div>You do realize that neither you nor I have actually detailed what we think &quot;using puppetry to assist a willing character&quot; would actually accomplish?<br /> <br /> So, that's a bold claim made without any understanding or attempt to be understood. Bad form.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Charcoal march of spiders almost did everything in one charm as well. </div> </div> </div>Two Charms, and they were broken as fuck, even as Martial Arts 5, Essence 4 Charms.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-28T07:08:26-07:00","id":1230802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1230171-razor-wire-gloves-artifact-or-martial-art?p=1230776#post1230776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it ENABLES them to defend you. A player character can choose not to apply their Parry against any particular attack; NPCs are not generally afforded that choice because they're storyteller characters and their autonomy is less important.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose that's true from a point of view.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If by &quot;forces&quot; you mean &quot;persuades&quot;. </div> </div> </div>It's a compulsion effect. There is no actual persuasion. It skips that with a successful roll and forces NPCs to spend willpower to break.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Completely irrelevant when there are no more &quot;hero styles&quot;!<br /> <br /> The base Style was complete already, and doesn't need a whole other Style tacked on. </div> </div> </div>But they still exist in brawl.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Chiyo wouldn't have been able to do that if Sakura had resisted.<br /> <br /> Therefore, the more powerful trick is using someone as a puppet when they don't want to be a puppet.<br /> <br /> You do realize that neither you nor I have actually detailed what we think &quot;using puppetry to assist a willing character&quot; would actually accomplish?<br /> <br /> So, that's a bold claim made without any understanding or attempt to be understood. Bad form. </div> </div> </div>In may's monthly, there is a demon called a Fulope. Which models it perfectly, I'm not sure if I'm allowed to copy paste that charm but it pretty much does almost everything. Though it's not for fighting that's specifically for singing but it could be reworked.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Two Charms, and they were broken as fuck, even as Martial Arts 5, Essence 4 Charms.<br /> </div> </div> </div>There were a lot of broken charms but those were fine last time I checked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-28T07:12:40-07:00","id":1230806,"title":"","content":"For Puppet Spider style, I\u2019d probably start with low level grapple enhancers, maybe stolen from Mantis or the Distaff, since you need to grab hold of people before you can puppet them. Introduce some kind of \u201cpuppet\u201d option of things you can do while grappling with the Form, then go in on higher level grapple enhancers, a \u201ccreate a wall of webs\u201d charm, and maybe finish off with an AoE grapple.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-28T09:17:18-07:00","id":1230833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1230171-razor-wire-gloves-artifact-or-martial-art?p=1230806#post1230806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Puppet Spider style, I\u2019d probably start with low level grapple enhancers, maybe stolen from Mantis or the Distaff, since you need to grab hold of people before you can puppet them. Introduce some kind of \u201cpuppet\u201d option of things you can do while grappling with the Form, then go in on higher level grapple enhancers, a \u201ccreate a wall of webs\u201d charm, and maybe finish off with an AoE grapple.</div> </div> </div> </div>No AoE grapple against anything but a battle group. Can you remember a string master who was able to restrain multiple heroes at once?<br /> <br /> I\u2019m thinking that the Form Charm allows you to grab and hold (\u201cready\u201d, if a weapon) as many objects as you have wire-using hands. Lunars with multiple arms can really get their Spider on. Those who can access Mastery level can control multiple things with just one hand, or at least more than two things with both hands. Those limited to the Terrestrial level need both hands to control one thing at a time.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind that holding multiple things is different from being able to take multiple actions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 06-28-2018, 12:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-29T07:07:29-07:00","id":1231096,"title":"","content":"Only Sidereals and Solars can practice Sidereals Martial Arts.<br /> <br /> Does anyone feel that Terrestrial, Lunar, Liminal, or Alchemical Exalted should not be capable of practicing a wire-based Martial Art Style?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-29T08:06:14-07:00","id":1231112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1230171-razor-wire-gloves-artifact-or-martial-art?p=1231096#post1231096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone feel that Terrestrial, Lunar, Liminal, or Alchemical Exalted should not be capable of practicing a wire-based Martial Art Style?</div> </div> </div> </div>Live Wire Style was already a thing in 2e.<br /> <br /> I think the more important question for it is, are <i>mortals</i> capable of practicing this as a martial arts style? Because as far as I recall, Joe Mortal McMonk probably doesn't have a non-magical means of slinging razor wires around to decapitate people at a distance, let alone do so and still have fingers afterward.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 06-29-2018, 11:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-29T10:12:49-07:00","id":1231141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1230171-razor-wire-gloves-artifact-or-martial-art?p=1231112#post1231112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Live Wire Style was already a thing in 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Despite the name, the weapons were whips and dire lashes.<br /> <br /> But admittedly, a fair number of these wire-users treat their strings as slicing whips.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think the more important question for it is, are <i>mortals</i> capable of practicing this as a martial arts style? Because as far as I recall, Joe Mortal McMonk probably doesn't have a non-magical means of slinging razor wires around to decapitate people at a distance, let alone do so and still have fingers afterward. </div> </div> </div>Robert has started the precedent of \u201cStyles for which mortals cannot even practice the fundamentals\u201d with Sublime Danger\u2019s Thousand Sword Style, and it was likely to happen with Sidereal Martial Arts anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-29T11:02:14-07:00","id":1231154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1230171-razor-wire-gloves-artifact-or-martial-art?p=1231096#post1231096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only Sidereals and Solars can practice Sidereals Martial Arts.<br /> <br /> Does anyone feel that Terrestrial, Lunar, Liminal, or Alchemical Exalted should not be capable of practicing a wire-based Martial Art Style?</div> </div> </div> </div>What exactly do you want from the style. How powerful do you want it to be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-29T12:26:32-07:00","id":1231180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1230171-razor-wire-gloves-artifact-or-martial-art?p=1231154#post1231154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What exactly do you want from the style. How powerful do you want it to be?</div> </div> </div> </div>I want it to be as available and accessible as it ought to be, and I\u2019ll tailor the power to that consideration.<br /> <br /> Terrestrial and Mastery effects allow for one avenue of variable power, as do native Charms, dice pools, artifacts from three dot ratings to N/A, the Dissonant and Resonant keywords, and the potential to gate certain Evocations behind native Exalted Charms.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s not even getting into totally unique powers arising from a spirit\u2019s natural Charms, or derived from an empowering sorcerous working.<br /> <br /> So, the question remains: Does anyone think there is any kind of Exalt who should be completely barred from this general body of combat techniques?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-29T16:16:36-07:00","id":1231248,"title":"","content":"I feel the style you're groping towards is fair game for everyone. Exalts might be able to infuse the wires with motion, but even a mortal can put piano wire on a shuriken, and rope darts and yo you oughta be in style here and those are both things mortal martial artists use in real life.<br /> <br /> Trainees probably work their way up to a full web from a single strand, adding one wire at a time and building up spacial awareness by navigating razor wire be-webbed rooms blindfolded by twanging a strand and listening to the notes.<br /> <br /> You gain more than you lose by letting mortals learn it, and gambits/tags can cover a lot of neat rope/wire tricks even for folks without charms. Picture a whole school run by these guys!<br /> <br /> Edit: A terrestrial/mastery tier does seem appropriate. A case could be made for air or earth, but I am not feeling a strong elemental affinity here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-29T21:57:31-07:00","id":1231300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1230171-razor-wire-gloves-artifact-or-martial-art?p=1231180#post1231180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want it to be as available and accessible as it ought to be, and I\u2019ll tailor the power to that consideration.<br /> <br /> Terrestrial and Mastery effects allow for one avenue of variable power, as do native Charms, dice pools, artifacts from three dot ratings to N/A, the Dissonant and Resonant keywords, and the potential to gate certain Evocations behind native Exalted Charms.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s not even getting into totally unique powers arising from a spirit\u2019s natural Charms, or derived from an empowering sorcerous working.<br /> <br /> So, the question remains: Does anyone think there is any kind of Exalt who should be completely barred from this general body of combat techniques?</div> </div> </div> </div>So how far do you want it? My only complaints arose from puppeteering because as I said, my mind drifts to then penultimate version of that, which i feel is not within the real of normal MA.<br /> <br /> I style that uses wires to control tools makes sense. Though, I can't see anything that would require finite control without essence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-30T12:55:57-07:00","id":1231420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1230171-razor-wire-gloves-artifact-or-martial-art?p=1231300#post1231300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My only complaints arose from puppeteering because as I said, my mind drifts to then penultimate version of that, which i feel is not within the real of normal MA.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I've said before, there are no shortage of wire-based artifact weapon ideas to use as receptacles for the strongest sorts of wire tricks, or at least the strongest expressions of the strongest tricks.<br /> <br /> Infinite Uses: Cross Tail (Akame ga Kill), Excelion (Black Cat), Black Rope (Basilisk), &quot;Seven Heavens Seven Blades&quot; Shichiten Shichitou (To Aru Majutsu no Index)... respectively moonsilver, orichalcum, green jade or something at least as resonant as green jade with Dragon-Blooded, and blue jade.<br /> <br /> Walter's wires were given no name, but they were also clearly not normal strands of fiber or metal. Not like the mundane musical strings that Kanzaki of <i>Get Backers</i> uses, even to defeat a rival student who used special alloy wires.<br /> <br /> Yura of the Hair (Inuyasha) used normal hair, but she was a spirit whose unique powers would more than compensate for that.<br /> <br /> Then there are those who don't use physical strings at all. Machi and Pitou (Hunter x Hunter), <i>Naruto </i>puppet ninjas, and possibly Touhou Project's Alice Margatroid all use Essence by other names to form their threads.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 06-30-2018, 04:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-01T15:11:13-07:00","id":1231669,"title":"","content":"Opinions on this idea? Using wires to ensnare a target at range is only <i>sometimes </i>actually modeled as a grapple gambit.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Withering</b> attacks can represent attempts to ensnare someone that fail to actually ensnare, but which at least force the target into less advantageous positions. These attacks can be supplemented with another Charm that destroys parts of the environment, as the wires close around roof-supporting pillars, trees, or the small bridge the target is standing upon. Creative destruction of the environment can force the target into even worse positions than modeled by Initiative loss from the withering attack. Perhaps model the attempt to avoid harm from such destruction as a reflexive check against an environmental hazard.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, the withering attacks can be supplemented by a Charm that changes the narrative; the attack <i>does </i>successfully ensnare the target, and the martial artist uses this to effectively make a Knockback-type Smashing attack, moving the target into another range band and inflicting withering damage from smashing them into walls or trees. Just as with the above option of destroying a bridge under their feet, this could subject a target to a lethal fall.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Decisive</b> attacks can narratively represent successful attempts to ensnare someone, but with the intent to immediately pull the threads taught and inflict damage. These attacks can be supplemented with another Charm that inflicts a crippling injury, slicing off fingers, toes, hands, feet, or entire limbs. The target is not actually clinched because they are set free as soon as damage is resolved.<br /> <br /> <br /> Actually using a grapple gambit to <i>mechanically</i> clinch someone outside of close range requires that the target be within close range of a sufficiently large, solid, immobile object against which wires can bind them, such as a boulder, tree, or pillar. The target suffers the usual penalties of a grapple, but cannot be fully Restrained (and certainly can't be Dragged), and so can attack or defend against anyone within close range. If the target or his ally can break the object to which they are bound, they are set free.<br /> <br /> The martial artist cannot benefit from Charms that preserve rounds of control in the face of being attacked or damaged. Further, it might take only a single successful attack even without damage to instantly break the martial artist's hold on the victim.<br /> <br /> The martial artist can execute withering or decisive Savaging attacks against the victim as normal, though possibly at a cost of two rounds per attack.<br /> <br /> Slam/Throw attacks might be impossible.<br /> <br /> The victim can spend their action struggling against the bindings without flurrying in order to reduce the rounds of control, but doing so might cause them Initiative loss as their struggles causes the wires to dig in. Crashed victims instead suffer health damage.<br /> <br /> Actions to struggle against the wires might also double as feats of strength actions to damage the object to which one is bound, so that a victim has two possible methods of getting free even without being able to attack the martial artist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-02T00:59:33-07:00","id":1231737,"title":"","content":"Another inspiration could be Lyra Orphee <a href=\"http://saintseiya.wikia.com/wiki/Lyra_Orph%C3%A9e\" target=\"_blank\">http://saintseiya.wikia.com/wiki/Lyra_Orph%C3%A9e</a> and Benetnasch Mime <a href=\"http://villains.wikia.com/wiki/Benetnasch_Eta_Mime\" target=\"_blank\">http://villains.wikia.com/wiki/Benetnasch_Eta_Mime</a> from Saint Seiya and their instrument based attacks:<br /> Stringer Requiem<br /> Stringer Nocturn<br /> Death Trap Serenade<br /> Stringer Fine<br /> <br /> Maybe much more Performance related than Martial arts","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12575-gaara","name":"Gaara","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-02T08:11:27-07:00","id":1231812,"title":"","content":"I'd like to have some feedback on my last post.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"116\" data-vbnamecard=\"116\">Epimetheus</a> had so much to say in fear of this Style being too strong without even seeing implementation; now's his chance to address some actual possibilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-02T20:56:59-07:00","id":1232039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1230171-razor-wire-gloves-artifact-or-martial-art?p=1231812#post1231812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to have some feedback on my last post.<br /> <br /> <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> had so much to say in fear of this Style being too strong without even seeing implementation; now's his chance to address some actual possibilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>My first question still remains what's the theme? What exactly are you trying to emulate?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-02T21:18:18-07:00","id":1232044,"title":"","content":"Clearly we expect different things from communication.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T01:32:54-07:00","id":1232067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1230171-razor-wire-gloves-artifact-or-martial-art?p=1232044#post1232044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clearly we expect different things from communication.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess. It just comes from the thought process. What is this style supposed to be? Just naming a list of effects doesn't help.In my opinion, trying to conform a bunch of possibly disparate abilities together, causes more issues than it solves. When I think about MA I first think about a theme, think of what those themes embody, and then come up with charms that embody those themes. Wire control is such a broad skill. Narrowing it down to something is generally preferable. Personally, if you want to use the themes of nature and one in which the focus is on trapping people, I'd consider something like a plant based vine style. If it's focused on killing people a wire it'd probably be an ideal like dreaming pearl does. There's also the possibility of using a spider but I feel it's always harder to create a style that technically already exists as an SMA. I can't help but feel like such a style would just be weakening and breaking up the already existing SMA. I could also see a puppet non-SMA but you'd probably have to keep it out of non-essence users because the style would probably revolve around using essence to control inanimate objects. Something that just doesn't seem possible without an essence pool. However, coming from an approach of effects first, doesn't seem very practical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T07:09:40-07:00","id":1232111,"title":"","content":"We shouldn't need to talk about themes to discuss the most balanced ways to model wire-snaring attacks in <i>Exalted</i>.<br /> <br /> There's no debate about whether such attacks will be in the game, either as a reprise of those Charcoal Spider Charms or as part of a different Style or as Evocations of an artifact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}